  "title": "Ratio spreads: avoid naked short units and judge each part alone",
  "summary": "Two points on ratio spreads. First, selling one extra unit leaves you outright short that unit, which is dangerous on margin; if you sell an extra put, make it cash-secured. Second, a ratio spread is two trades in one, like a zebra (buy two ITM calls, sell one ATM call). Evaluate each part alone and only do the good one.",
